    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="82">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:IICn">II Cn</ref> 82</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="82" corresp="#wit-g-a">⁊ ic wylle, þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> ælc man si griðes wyrðe to gemote ⁊ fram gemote, butan he si æbǽre þeof.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="82" corresp="#wit-a">⁊ ic wille, þæt ælc man sy griðes wyrðe to gemote ⁊ fram gemote, buton he æbære þeof sy.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="82" corresp="#wit-q">Et uolo, ut omnis homo pacem habeat eundo ad gemotum uel rediens de gemoto (id est placito), nisi probatus fur sit.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#robertson" n="82" corresp="#wit-b">And ic wille þæt ælc man beo griðes wyrðe to gemote ⁊ fram gemote, buton he æbere ðeof beo.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a">And ic wylle þæt ælc man si griðes wyrðe to gemote and fram gemote, butan he si æbære þeof.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-b">And it is my will that every man shall be entitled to protection in going to and from assemblies, unless he be a notorious thief.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a">And it is my will that everyone shall be entitled to protection on the way to and from assemblies unless he is a known thief.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#whitelock">And it is my will that every man is to be entitled to peace, going to a meeting and from a meeting, unless he is a manifest thief.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann">Und ich will, dass jedermann besonderen Friedensschutzes theilhaftig sei [auf dem Wege] zum Gericht und vom Gericht, wenn er nicht ein unleugbarer Dieb ist.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">And I will that every man be entitled to special peace-protection [on the way] to the court and from the court, unless he is an undeniable thief.</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#liebermann" n="366"><ref target="clause:IIIAtr_1">III Atr 1</ref></note>
        <note type="comparisonPrinted" source="#liebermann">ebd. 1</note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#wormald-mel" n="359"><label>loose/partial source (in parentheses)</label> <ref target="clause:IIIAtr_1">III Atr 1–1.2</ref> <quote>Table 5.4, II Cn 82: (III Atr 1-1:2)</quote></note>
